WhatsApp Coexistence lets you connect your existing WhatsApp Business app number
to AutoWaba — without giving up the app. After connecting, you can send
high-volume campaigns and automated messages through AutoWaba, while still
handling 1:1 conversations directly in the WhatsApp Business app. Both sides
stay in sync.

{% video src="/videos/autowaba-whatsapp-coexistence.mp4" %}{% /video %}

## Before you start — does your number qualify?

Meta only allows Coexistence if **all** of these are true:

- Your WhatsApp Business app is version **2.24.17 or newer** — update from the app store first
- The number has been **actively used in the WhatsApp Business app for at least 7 days** — new or barely-used numbers are refused
- The number was **not recently moved** from another WhatsApp Business Account or provider — recently migrated numbers have a cooldown period
- The number is on the **WhatsApp Business app**, not the regular WhatsApp app
- The number is from a **country where Meta supports Coexistence** — check [Meta's Coexistence guide](https://www.facebook.com/business/help) if unsure

## How the connection works

When you go through the AutoWaba connection flow, you'll see an option to
connect your existing WhatsApp Business app account instead of registering a
fresh number. Here's what happens:

1. Enter your WhatsApp Business app phone number
2. WhatsApp sends a **verification code** to your WhatsApp Business app via the
   official Facebook Business Account — tap **Connect** on that message
3. Tap **Connect to the Business Platform**, then **Confirm**
4. Paste the verification code back into the flow
5. Done — your number is now connected to AutoWaba

## What changes after connecting

| Feature | After connecting |
|---|---|
| 1:1 chats | Work on both AutoWaba and the WA Business app — messages are mirrored |
| Contacts | Fully synced |
| Group chats | Stay on the WA Business app only — not available via AutoWaba |
| Broadcast lists | Disabled — existing lists become read-only |
| Disappearing & view-once messages | Turned off for all 1:1 chats |
| Voice & video calls | No change — WA Business app only |
| Business profile & catalog | No change — WA Business app only |

## A few limitations to know

**Throughput is capped at 20 messages per second** for numbers using Coexistence
— lower than a standard Cloud API number. For most businesses this is plenty,
but keep it in mind for very large campaign sends.

Group chats are not supported on the Cloud API side. Everything sent and
received in group chats stays in the WhatsApp Business app and won't appear in
AutoWaba.

## Pricing

Messages you send from the **WhatsApp Business app** continue to be **free**.
Messages sent via **AutoWaba (Cloud API)** are billed at standard WhatsApp
Cloud API rates — the same pricing that applies to any other AutoWaba number.

## How to disconnect

If you ever need to disconnect, you do it from the **WhatsApp Business app**
directly — not from AutoWaba. Go to **Settings → Account → Business Platform**
and tap **Disconnect Account**. AutoWaba will be notified automatically.

